WEBVTT

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:05.560
Give us permission to release 
the limit on the Prafka.

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:08.220
That's why I was made.

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:14.490
You must stop Red Shift from activating.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:16.530
Go!

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:19.060
Thank you!

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:22.420
Let's go, Inia.

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:23.170
Yeah!

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:27.380
I've been waiting for this!

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:29.570
For this moment!

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:48.060
<b>White Darkness</b>

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:24.910
The dolls are finally mine!

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:30.000
The day when the Master's Last Battalion 
shall destroy the world is nigh!

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:33.490
The world?

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:37.170
You bastard...!

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:39.300
Hey, dolls.

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:43.430
Before you destroy the world, 
start by taking care of that fly!

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:46.330
Destroy the world.

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:49.100
Destroy. Protect.

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:52.560
Protect Yuuya's world...

00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:54.860
What are you doing?! Kill them!

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:56.280
He'll be killed.

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:59.070
Yuuya will die.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:05.660
What?

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:13.830
What?

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:24.650
What the hell is going on?

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:26.810
What's happening?

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:03.800
Splendid! Simply splendid!

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:06.520
This is the Nastroyka Effect. {Thanks to Ukrainian buddy for helping with Russian! I guess it means like "To set a clock."}

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:08.970
I was right!

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:12.620
Yuuya Bridges is the ultimate catalyst!

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:20.970
Wh-

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:29.790
This is Infinity 1.

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:31.160
Can you hear me?

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:34.040
Captain! If you're close enough 
for communications, then...

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:36.790
Yes, we're managing with the Laser Class...

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:42.300
We'll meet up with you soon.

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:45.560
Can you hear me, Argos 1?

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:47.540
We're heading there now.

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:48.800
You're okay?

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:50.970
Wait, why are you...

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:52.540
We're borrowing their Assault Cannons,

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:55.000
and we're all taking down the 
Heavy Laser Class together.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:57.880
You follow the BETA that escaped.

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:01.190
Watch my back. Don't let 
a single one through.

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:04.150
You think we can't handle it? Go!

00:05:30.170 --> 00:05:32.310
Damn it! The right flank's not holding!

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:34.930
You took over the Comms center, right?

00:05:35.170 --> 00:05:38.190
Somebody get over here! I don't 
care if you're Soviet or American!

00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:44.190
But even if the base responded immediately 
there's no guarantee they'll make it in time.

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:47.950
What is this?

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:50.320
That leader unit from before?

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:54.950
There's no way he beat 
the Scarlet Twins, right?

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:57.710
The Scarlet Twins...

00:05:58.210 --> 00:05:59.180
What?

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:00.680
No way!

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:03.460
Are they inside that thing?

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:13.720
This is Argos 1! White Fang! Argos 2!

00:06:14.170 --> 00:06:16.890
Cryska! Inia! Lt. Sandek!

00:06:18.050 --> 00:06:20.480
Damn it! Somebody answer me!

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:25.130
That's...

00:06:32.920 --> 00:06:34.020
Tarisa?

00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:36.010
You bastards!

00:06:36.010 --> 00:06:36.700
Stay away!

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:39.020
You follow the BETA!

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:41.970
What's going on?

00:06:41.970 --> 00:06:46.560
Is that TSF the same one we were fighting?

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:47.340
That's right.

00:06:47.780 --> 00:06:49.840
This is our enemy.

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:51.460
Enemy...

00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:52.600
Then we should fight it together!

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:54.020
Calm down, Bridges.

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:56.600
Our priority now is preventing the Red Shift!

00:06:57.160 --> 00:06:58.600
Bridges...

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:00.650
You need to save America,

00:07:00.650 --> 00:07:03.360
your homeland, from destruction!

00:07:04.660 --> 00:07:07.880
While you still have the chance...

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:08.360
But...!

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:10.680
I'll be fine.

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:15.120
I've seen plenty of melee combat 
when I was in the Empire.

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:21.400
Now it's your turn to believe in me, Yuuya.

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:23.170
Yuuya?

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:51.900
I can't let Yuuya be the one to kill them.

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:11.510
Yui!

00:08:15.380 --> 00:08:17.290
Now it's after me?

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:21.760
Alright. I'll fight you!

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:22.840
Wait, Bridges!

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:26.210
Can you hear me, Ensign Bridges?

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:28.180
Lt. Sandek?

00:08:29.370 --> 00:08:30.600
Listen to me.

00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:32.920
The pilots of that TSF...

00:08:32.920 --> 00:08:34.240
No, Yuuya!

00:08:35.420 --> 00:08:36.480
Yuuya...

00:08:38.340 --> 00:08:39.960
You can't mean...

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:42.750
Yes. It's Ensigns Barchenowa and Sestina.

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:49.380
What the hell?

00:08:49.780 --> 00:08:54.130
What are they doing in there...? 
Why are they attacking us?

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:56.810
My guess is MK Ultra.

00:08:56.810 --> 00:09:00.940
A type of brainwashing that uses 
drugs and powerful hypnosis.

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:02.490
MK Ultra?

00:09:02.810 --> 00:09:04.140
The CIA!

00:09:04.570 --> 00:09:07.140
Then America is behind this?

00:09:07.140 --> 00:09:08.570
I don't know that.

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:11.650
But hypnotic suggestion can be undone.

00:09:12.210 --> 00:09:15.650
And you're the only one who can do that.

00:09:15.960 --> 00:09:17.260
Ensign Bridges!

00:09:27.740 --> 00:09:30.980
They've been responding to 
any words that involve you.

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:35.510
It appears to be some kind of key, 
given how interested they were in you.

00:09:37.570 --> 00:09:39.890
Even if it's a slim hope,

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:42.170
it's our only bet.

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:46.940
If we can't, not only will we 
not be able to stop the BETA,

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:49.260
that TSF will kill us.

00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:51.400
I won't let you!

00:09:59.810 --> 00:10:01.260
Cryska! Inia!

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:02.910
It's me! Yuuya!

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:05.250
Please, wake up!

00:10:06.120 --> 00:10:09.540
Stop it, Yuuya! There's no 
evidence for what he's saying!

00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:12.040
We don't know until we try!

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:15.050
Don't turn away from 
reality! They're already...

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:16.420
Shut up!

00:10:17.370 --> 00:10:19.340
Life's never been easy!

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:21.590
What you abandon, and what you take...

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:27.320
Even I know that repeating that 
choice is what it means to be alive!

00:10:27.850 --> 00:10:28.740
But still!

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:31.650
If that means I have to keep losing 
everything over and over...

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:35.210
I'll risk my life to try and take it all!

00:10:35.210 --> 00:10:37.970
I won't give up! Ever!

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:39.610
Yuuya...

00:10:40.690 --> 00:10:42.540
That's right. Just like that.

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:47.370
It's true that there is no other possibility.

00:10:47.850 --> 00:10:51.740
My guess is that the shock 
of killing Bridges themselves

00:10:51.740 --> 00:10:55.380
is the only way to bring the 
dolls back under our control.

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:05.560
Cryska! Inia! Listen to me!

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:10.310
I feel like since I've come here I've 
finally started to walk my own path.

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:17.850
And that's because everyone 
here accepted me for who I was.

00:11:19.660 --> 00:11:21.820
So now it's my turn!

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:29.330
I want to give back to you what I was given!

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:31.660
What?

00:11:33.340 --> 00:11:34.170
No way...

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:35.900
Yuuya!

00:11:42.890 --> 00:11:45.490
No!

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:12.740
I...

00:12:13.360 --> 00:12:14.920
What did I...

00:12:16.330 --> 00:12:18.730
Are you okay, Cryska?

00:12:25.620 --> 00:12:27.300
I finally got it.

00:12:27.700 --> 00:12:29.820
Yuuya! Are you okay?

00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:32.310
Yeah. I think so.

00:12:35.570 --> 00:12:40.440
This wasn't planned, but it turned 
out well for me nonetheless.

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:43.070
Inia! Inia!

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:45.940
Wake up! Please! Inia!

00:12:45.940 --> 00:12:48.100
No, don't try to move her.

00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:49.830
Please! Save her, Yuuya!

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:51.280
I know!

00:12:51.280 --> 00:12:52.260
I'll take her vitals.

00:12:52.260 --> 00:12:53.580
I'm sorry, Inia.

00:12:53.970 --> 00:12:55.210
I'm sorry.

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:59.440
I said that we'd protect Yuuya's 
world together... But...

00:12:59.890 --> 00:13:00.760
I...

00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:02.340
My world?

00:13:02.930 --> 00:13:04.010
Yuuya...

00:13:04.740 --> 00:13:06.440
What should I do?

00:13:06.920 --> 00:13:09.300
Inia... Inia!

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:10.350
It's okay.

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:13.770
Inia always comes back, right?

00:13:19.080 --> 00:13:21.410
American Air Force bombers.

00:13:22.130 --> 00:13:25.520
It seems the world is saved.

00:13:33.460 --> 00:13:35.690
Look for survivors!

00:13:36.700 --> 00:13:38.810
I thought the odds were pretty bad...

00:13:39.210 --> 00:13:41.340
But I guess that's why 
gambling's so hard to quit.

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:48.100
Those who believed in their choices 
and potential until the very end

00:13:48.700 --> 00:13:51.540
found the thin thread 
that leads to the future.

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:53.960
That's what I believe.

00:13:55.040 --> 00:14:00.480
And that's the answer I couldn't find.

00:14:11.480 --> 00:14:13.610
You got greedy, Christopher.

00:14:21.640 --> 00:14:23.290
Now it's time to move on.

00:14:36.210 --> 00:14:41.280
Borning was a huge help this time.

00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:43.820
Not at all. We did what anyone would do.

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:47.820
The fates of my company and your 
plan are inexorably linked.

00:14:48.460 --> 00:14:52.140
And these events were an excellent 
advertisement to the rest of the world

00:14:52.140 --> 00:14:55.440
for the necessity of having TSFs.

00:14:55.890 --> 00:14:56.830
Yes.

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:05.050
A UN Military Spokesman gave the total 
number of casualties for the Yukon terrorist attacks

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:08.490
as 2312, as of today, the 25th.

00:15:08.490 --> 00:15:12.290
There are also over 1400 missing.

00:15:13.770 --> 00:15:19.740
Also, regarding the secret treaty between the 
US and Soviet governments revealed by the RLF,

00:15:19.740 --> 00:15:25.450
the so-called "Red Shift", the African Union and 
Oceania, permanent members of the UN security council,

00:15:25.450 --> 00:15:28.740
issued a joint announcement 
calling for a UN investigation.

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:32.990
It just doesn't seem right.

00:15:33.400 --> 00:15:35.440
What are you talking about?

00:15:35.440 --> 00:15:39.490
Your machine got scrapped, aren't you 
glad you weren't hurt worse?

00:15:39.490 --> 00:15:41.120
Like hell I am!

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:43.090
Those sisters got me again!

00:15:43.090 --> 00:15:44.500
Damn it!

00:15:44.970 --> 00:15:49.160
We don't even know what's 
going to happen to us now!

00:15:49.160 --> 00:15:50.370
Hey, Chihuahua.

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:54.510
I was nice enough to visit you, 
don't make this all depressing.

00:15:55.160 --> 00:15:56.740
I'm sorry, Lieutenant.

00:15:57.480 --> 00:16:00.400
A lot happened really suddenly.

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:03.140
I've heard.

00:16:03.540 --> 00:16:06.150
Takamura's being sent back to Japan.

00:16:06.620 --> 00:16:08.400
I heard that they're planning 
on shutting down the project

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:10.980
because of the losses we suffered.

00:16:12.210 --> 00:16:17.420
It's possible that Lt. Takamura 
might not even come back.

00:16:17.420 --> 00:16:19.570
Does Yuuya know that?

00:16:20.380 --> 00:16:22.480
He should.

00:16:22.480 --> 00:16:25.840
He's calmer than you'd expect.

00:16:25.840 --> 00:16:26.930
I see.

00:16:30.540 --> 00:16:34.180
I'm sure it's hitting 
him harder than anybody.

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:38.680
You're working awfully hard for 
somebody who's leaving soon.

00:16:39.320 --> 00:16:41.970
My luggage is all taken care of,

00:16:41.970 --> 00:16:45.680
but I wanted to at least 
leave storage instructions.

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:47.000
I see.

00:16:48.060 --> 00:16:50.320
It's still awfully sudden.

00:16:50.730 --> 00:16:52.660
The stated reason for my being called home

00:16:52.660 --> 00:16:56.780
is so I can give the details 
on the terrorist attack,

00:16:57.680 --> 00:17:02.760
but it's mostly going to a public hearing on 
whether the XFJ project should be continued,

00:17:02.760 --> 00:17:04.290
and then a court of inquiry.

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:07.930
Stopping the BETA from reaching Red Shift,

00:17:07.930 --> 00:17:10.020
and defeating the USSR's latest TSF.

00:17:10.560 --> 00:17:12.860
The opponents of the project are 
going to use these two successes

00:17:12.860 --> 00:17:15.420
as justification for saying it's complete.

00:17:16.050 --> 00:17:20.600
And then they're planning on stopping 
it during the domestic trial run phase.

00:17:21.090 --> 00:17:25.100
So have you said goodbye 
to the rest of your squad?

00:17:25.100 --> 00:17:27.060
No. There's no need to.

00:17:28.300 --> 00:17:31.940
I'm coming back for sure.

00:17:33.980 --> 00:17:35.120
I see.

00:17:40.340 --> 00:17:43.280
I'll keep the project going no matter what.

00:17:43.280 --> 00:17:46.100
From now on, that's my fight.

00:17:56.370 --> 00:17:58.720
They sent her back to Japan before 
she could be assassinated?

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:00.370
That's fine.

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:03.720
I'll eliminate anyone who 
gets in the way of my plan,

00:18:04.480 --> 00:18:06.480
no matter who they may be.

00:18:09.170 --> 00:18:12.090
You don't want to see Yuuya before we leave?

00:18:13.040 --> 00:18:15.730
We'll see him again on some 
battlefield or another.

00:18:16.410 --> 00:18:18.840
It looks like I'm stuck with him.

00:18:33.620 --> 00:18:36.900
Lt. Takamura is leaving soon.

00:18:37.740 --> 00:18:38.320
Yeah.

00:18:38.970 --> 00:18:40.940
You don't want to go see her?

00:18:41.280 --> 00:18:43.690
You may never see her again.

00:18:43.690 --> 00:18:45.530
Yui will come back.

00:18:47.530 --> 00:18:50.560
The Shiranui she and I made is here.

00:18:51.320 --> 00:18:52.920
So she'll come back.

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:55.780
I know it.

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:02.840
When did that start?

00:19:03.770 --> 00:19:07.650
When did you start calling 
the 94 Second the Shiranui?

00:19:09.100 --> 00:19:14.570
The old you would've never used 
a Japanese name like that.

00:19:15.160 --> 00:19:16.260
That's true.

00:19:17.620 --> 00:19:19.330
When, I wonder?

00:19:48.650 --> 00:19:49.450
Yuuya.

00:20:08.380 --> 00:20:09.010
Y-

00:20:13.360 --> 00:20:17.740
My job is to make the 94 
Second the perfect machine!

00:21:35.130 --> 00:21:36.690
Ensign Barchenowa...

00:21:39.330 --> 00:21:40.780
Lt. Takamura.

00:21:42.160 --> 00:21:44.190
There's...

00:21:49.090 --> 00:21:52.200
There's something I have to tell you.

00:23:29.370 --> 00:23:31.680
I see. I thought so.

00:23:32.570 --> 00:23:35.410
This makes us enemies, doesn't it?

00:23:37.180 --> 00:23:39.000
We aren't enemies.

00:23:39.600 --> 00:23:42.190
Our position is more complicated 
and difficult than that.

00:23:43.160 --> 00:23:45.440
A more difficult enemy than any other?

00:23:46.180 --> 00:23:48.170
If you know, tell me.

00:23:48.170 --> 00:23:50.440
What do you call such a thing?

00:23:54.890 --> 00:23:56.180
Rivals in love.
